diff --git a/docs/gateway/config-tools/github-identity.md b/docs/gateway/config-tools/github-identity.md
index 45403a1b54a1e4f211c1ff72ae46f8ff00a1b21c..34aa97a8ff2d22011ac3d03a99d956cb8d44bca6 100644
--- a/docs/gateway/config-tools/github-identity.md
+++ b/docs/gateway/config-tools/github-identity.md
@@ -9,6 +9,21 @@ title: "Configuration — GitHub identity for agent tools"
 
 `tools.github` selects the shared managed GitHub CLI identity used by agent execution, and defines which execution paths receive its credential.
 
+## Distribution policy
+
+`OPENCLAW_NO_GITHUB=1` disables the built-in GitHub integration for the Gateway
+process. Set it before startup and restart the Gateway after changing it. Native
+account linking, publication, authenticated previews, PR discovery, remote GitHub
+project imports and their RPCs/tools are unavailable; their Control UI entries are
+hidden. OAuth refresh and managed-profile cleanup do not start, and retained
+`tools.github` selections do not inject credentials or Git authorship into tools.
+
+Ordinary Git/`gh` commands and separately supplied credentials remain usable.
+Existing account records are preserved. Preview-secret exclusions still apply to
+agent execution, and shared credentials used by login identity verification keep
+their existing validation. This policy does not restrict trusted shell code from
+using GitHub. The remaining sections describe behavior when integration is enabled.
+
 ## `tools.github`
 
 GitHub CLI identity is native by default. When `tools.github` is omitted, local agent tools, the Codex harness, and Agent Settings follow normal `gh` resolution: `GH_TOKEN` or `GITHUB_TOKEN` from the Gateway process takes precedence, followed by the runtime user's `gh` keyring/config. The Git author comes from the selected agent's workspace.
